    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="1a7aac32-a384-5387-be4b-afbf6fb97e03" activityNameId="9ea1525b-1fce-5c49-97aa-2844bc1a9580" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx 4-methyl-2-pentanone, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx 4-methyl-2-pentanone, at plant
The process "4-methyl-2-pentanone, at plant, RER" is modelled for the production of 4-methyl-2-pentanone from acetone in Europe. Raw materials, auxilliaries, energy consumptions and emissions are modelled with data from US-production.  Infrastructure and transports are calculated with standard values.;
CAS number: 000108-10-1; 
Formula: C6H12O; 
Synonyms: methyl isobutyl ketone; 
UUID: 6931fb2e-057d-3510-bdaa-539c0fd13f41
Production of 4-methyl-2-pentanone including materials, energy uses, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Europe.
Technology: Hydrgenation of acetone
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: Total production in the world  is around 380.000 tons.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Transports are modelled with standard distances.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6931fb2e-057d-3510-bdaa-539c0fd13f41.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
